<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  Auto Backup on Android 11 and below.

  Empty on purpose. `android:allowBackup="false"` in the manifest already disables Auto
  Backup outright, so nothing here is consulted — the file stays because the manifest
  attribute still points at it and because deleting it would make the next person wonder
  whether backup was considered.

  On the encryption: an Auto Backup of this database would be useless as well as unwanted.
  The SQLCipher passphrase is wrapped by an Android Keystore key that cannot be exported or
  restored to another device, so a restored database would be an unopenable blob. Backing up
  a health worker's beneficiary records to a consumer cloud account is the reason it is off;
  that it would not even work is the second reason.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
